            <ArticleTitle>The menopausal woman: The need for an individualized plan of care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-49</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000526765.60971.37</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>With life expectancy increasing, women will spend one-third of their lives in and beyond menopause. A collaborative discussion with the clinician facilitates informed decision-making and should include evidence-based discussion of physiologic changes, assessment of symptoms and treatment options, review of screening recommendations, and discussion of disease risk-reduction strategies and psychosocial issues.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
